1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
How to make a pocket pocket strap

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Tips and Tricks

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Hi, everyone. This is Tips and Tricks.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Today, I will show you how to make a pocket pocket strap.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Like the pocket pocket, we also use the pocket pocket to make a pocket pocket strap.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
We can see the effect of the pocket pocket strap on the pocket pocket strap.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Here is a real hole-in-the-box effect made by using duplicate simulation.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
In the case of duplicate simulation, there is a mutual effect between the board and the duplicate.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Currently, duplicate simulation can only be used in CPU simulation.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
So if you need to use duplicate simulation, it is recommended to switch to CPU simulation.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
We can see the hole-in-the-box effect on the left side.

12
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
It is to pass a complete rope through this duplicate.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Next, we need to pass this rope on the right side through a wooden buckle.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:11,000
In order to make it easier to operate, it is recommended that you first divide this rope into three parts.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
You can use the hook and loop tool to divide the board.

16
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Divide it into three parts here.

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
It is also to make it easier to pass through the board.

18
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Then add a fixed pin on the divided board.

19
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
And turn on simulation.

20
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Then add a fixed pin here.

21
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
It is to make it easier to adjust the shape of the board and the position of the moving board.

22
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Next, add a wooden buckle.

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
If you already have a corresponding duplicate solution,

24
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
you can add it.

25
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,000
You can also find a similar component in CLOAD library or CONNECT.

26
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Add it to the 3D window and use it.

27
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Then here, we can copy the wooden buckle that we already have in the object window.

28
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,000
And drag it into the 3D window to add it.

29
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Here, we can use the positioning ball directly.

30
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Adjust the position of the wooden buckle through the positioning ball.

31
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Make the top board pass through the ring in the wooden buckle.

32
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:33,000
You can see that this board has actually passed through the wooden buckle.

33
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
So you can turn on simulation.

34
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Look at its buckle effect.

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,000
You can see that the board and the duplicate are mutually effective at this time.

36
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
The board will hang the duplicate.

37
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Like the real buckle effect.

38
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
We need to pay attention to duplicate simulation.

39
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
The board has a conflict between the duplicate and the duplicate.

40
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Therefore, in the process of making,

41
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
if the board and the duplicate pass through,

42
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,000
you can use the selection tool to adjust the board to pass through.

43
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Prevent simulation from the conflict between the board and the duplicate.

44
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
If you see the area where there is a pass through,

45
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
you can use the selection tool to select it.

46
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,000
And use the positioning ball to adjust its position.

47
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:20,000
So, the upper part of the wooden buckle is done.

48
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Then we wear the upper part of the wooden buckle.

49
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
You can adjust the remaining two parts of this strap.

50
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Because we have increased the thickness of the board.

51
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,000
To make it easier to look at.

52
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
The looping effect of the wooden buckle.

53
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
You can switch to the clothing suspension type.

54
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Switch to the texture surface.

55
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Then here.

56
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,000
We can see the pass-through effect of not only the thickness of the suspension.

57
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Let me remind you here.

58
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
If there is a deformation in the simulation process,

59
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
it can also be adjusted in the right-hand attribute editor.

60
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Adjust its rigidity.

61
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
The larger the rigidity, the more difficult it is to deform the duplicate.

62
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
You can also adjust the thickness of the conflict.

63
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,000
You can adjust the size of the gap between the duplicate and the board.

64
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Then make the looping effect of the strap.

65
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:14,000
We can arrange this small board in the position of the looping on the wooden buckle.

66
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
And adjust its position through the positioning ball.

67
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Make it pass through the wooden buckle on one side.

68
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
You can also switch to a different angle.

69
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Check the effect of the board.

70
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Here we have arranged the position on one side.

71
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
We can add a inner line to it here.

72
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Folding arrangement.

73
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
You can click on the 3D window.

74
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Then use the internal multidirectional line tool.

75
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Draw a inner line.

76
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Then select the folding arrangement tool in the 3D window.

77
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Select the inner line to fold.

78
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Then at the bottom.

79
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
You can also add a new inner line and fold it.

80
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Arrangement.

81
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
You can check whether there is a surface area.

82
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
If there is, you can adjust the folding angle.

83
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:01,000
At this time, the effect of this front buckle is also done.

84
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Then we can put the other two side boards.

85
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
In the state of opening the simulation.

86
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Use the fixed needle.

87
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Move its board position to the part that needs to be connected together.

88
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Got it!

89
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Then we can remove all the pins on the board.

90
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Then we can remove all the pins on the board.

91
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Ok...

92
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Tumbing the board together.

93
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Get ready forJa title.

94
00:05:48,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Open the simulation, check the cross-section of the board and the component, and adjust the cross-section area between the board and the component by selecting the grid tool.

95
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:28,000
You can also select the cross-section area in the 2D window frame, and adjust the location of the area by locating the ball.

96
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:33,000
In this way, the effect of the cross-section of the board and the component is done.

97
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Since the rope belt is a complete board, we need to merge these three boards together to form a complete belt.

98
00:06:44,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Here you can also change the angle of these two cross-section lines to 180 degrees, or delete these two internal lines.

99
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Finally, you can render the clothing type,

100
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
and change it to the surface of the dense pattern.

101
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:21,000
In this way, the thickness of the rope belt can also be displayed.

102
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Let's start the simulation again.

103
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:30,000
In this way, the whole adjustment belt, the real effect of the cross-section, is also done.

